Compile pk2cmd for 64-bit Windows with mingw-w64.

"Windows.h" only resolves on case-insensitive filesystems; the lowercase
spelling builds on both. The PATH search and the string copies pass the
buffer sizes the CRT secure functions want, keeping the three-argument
shims for Linux. The HID handle compares against INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE,
which holds on 64-bit where truncating the handle to int does not. The
hex writer funnels every host through one strncat spelling instead of
the platform secure name. To be offered upstream by the human so the
queue can shrink.

